comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T19:16:04.867Z",codex-jellyfin,Highest-priority requirement accepted. Current Bun coverage reports only functions and lines; evaluating LCOV/four-dimension enforcement and coverage capture for command subprocesses before selecting the non-cheatable gate.
  "2026-07-21T19:52:49.060Z",codex-jellyfin,Coverage remains the principal release blocker. Bun coverage reports 58.83% lines and 44.93% functions; Vitest can express all four 100% thresholds but its Node runtime currently fails 254 tests across 14 Bun-specific suites using Bun.spawn or Bun.serve. No artificial exclusions or mocked coverage inflation will be accepted.
  "2026-07-21T20:04:29.442Z",codex-jellyfin,"Latest post-change coverage run: 901 pass, 177 live-only skips, 0 fail; 58.64% lines and 44.56% functions. Command callbacks execute primarily in subprocess acceptance tests and are not attributed to the parent Bun coverage profile, which is the dominant instrumentation gap."
  "2026-07-22T04:41:08.659Z",codex-jellyfin,"Continuing implementation on 2026-07-22 after full all-status inventory; will measure current exact coverage first, close meaningful gaps, and verify read-only installed-binary E2E against the private configured instance."
  "2026-07-22T04:50:16.913Z",codex-jellyfin,"Portability foundation completed: typed Node adapters make 894 deterministic tests pass under Vitest; authoritative four-metric baseline is 38.19 statements, 37.40 branches, 49.92 functions, 37.87 lines. Live compiled CLI read-only suite passed 177/177. Item remains in progress because genuine 100/100/100/100 is not met."
  "2026-07-23T04:51:19.423Z",codex-jellyfin,"2026-07-23 continuation: full all-status PM lineage, live GitHub state, official Jellyfin sources, and private-profile boundaries reviewed. Measuring exact current four-metric gaps before adding behavior-focused tests; no exclusions or threshold weakening."
  "2026-07-23T05:14:21.420Z",codex-jellyfin,"2026-07-23 diagnostic after official TOON work: portable Vitest gate passes 906/906 with 38.24% statements, 37.38% branches, 50.00% functions, and 37.90% lines. The 100/100/100/100 acceptance requirement remains open and is not claimed complete."
  "2026-08-05T19:39:47.768Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260805,"2026-08-05 measurement from jf-935b: Vitest coverage is 42.22% statements, 42.30% branches, 52.43% functions, and 41.96% lines. The new coverage classification is directly unit-tested and schema-validated, but the repository-wide 100% goal remains open and was not claimed by this tranche."
  "2026-08-05T20:51:53.359Z",codex,"2026-08-05 measurement from jf-36oy: statements 43.36%, branches 44.01%, functions 54.11%, lines 43.18%; 978 portable tests passed with 1 skip. Goal remains open and was not claimed."
  "2026-08-06T18:11:25.731Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"2026-08-06 measurement from jf-einj: 996 portable tests passed with 1 skip; statements 43.76%, branches 44.86%, functions 54.37%, and lines 43.51%. New current-contract behaviors have focused assertions and live acceptance, but the repository-wide 100/100/100/100 goal remains open and was not claimed."
  "2026-08-06T18:30:28.097Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260806,"Final 2026-08-06 jf-einj measurement after read-only safety regressions: 999 portable tests passed with 1 skip; statements 43.78%, branches 44.87%, functions 54.37%, and lines 43.53%. The repository-wide 100/100/100/100 mandate remains open."
  "2026-08-07T05:28:00.519Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"2026-08-07 exact jf-einj measurement: 1001 portable tests passed with 1 intentional skip; statements 43.85%, branches 45.01%, functions 54.37%, lines 43.59%. The four-axis command exits zero because thresholds are not yet configured, so the non-bypassable 100/100/100/100 acceptance gate remains open and must not be represented as green."
  "2026-08-07T16:39:28.264Z",codex-jellyfin-coverage-20260807,"2026-08-07 run started after reading all 48 full PM items, the 601-entry lineage summarized by the prior closeout, current 48-node/137-edge graph, active blockers, release state, and all-status duplicate audit. This run claims only jf-mkzh; jf-lpki remains open and blocked. First decision is to measure missing coverage by production file and solve child-process attribution without ignore directives, exclusions, threshold weakening, or execution-only tests."
  "2026-08-09T21:26:45.132Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260809,"2026-08-09 implementation cycle: refreshed all-status PM inventory, complete active hierarchy, dependency graph, prior API/coverage plans, current Git/PR state, PM npm latest (2026.8.9), and official Jellyfin releases. This item is the sole actively claimed work because genuine 100/100/100/100 coverage is the canonical remaining release blocker and is directly coupled to safe API enhancement. I will measure current uncovered production paths, pair coverage with meaningful contract behavior, keep live validation strictly read-only, and preserve honest repo-wide totals."
  "2026-08-09T21:33:28.866Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260809,"Live 10.11.11 research found official read-only operation coverage at 249/249 but eight safe tools were left for manual fuzzy review. Five are wrapper names for documented GET operations; two use supported legacy routes omitted from the official OpenAPI; setup validate is multi-operation orchestration. Implemented exact wrapper contracts plus explicit non-endpoint reasons, eliminating read-only unmatched tools from 8 to 0 without increasing claimed operation coverage or making any live mutation."
notes[7]:
  - created_at: "2026-07-16T17:00:03.971Z"
    author: codex
    text: "Baseline from bun test --coverage on 2026-07-16: 888 pass,177 credential-dependent E2E skip,44.69% functions,59.26% lines; changed session formatter 100% functions and lines."
  - created_at: "2026-07-21T19:13:34.272Z"
    author: codex-jellyfin
    text: "Baseline measured with bun test --coverage on 2026-07-21: 898 pass, 177 skipped, 0 fail; 44.93% functions and 58.83% lines. Bun's text reporter exposes only functions/lines, so the mandatory gate must use a four-dimension instrumenter and per-file thresholds while preserving Bun compatibility."
  - created_at: "2026-07-21T19:52:50.098Z"
    author: codex-jellyfin
    text: "Decision: retain this feature in progress until genuine 100/100/100/100 source coverage is demonstrated. The next implementation step is a runtime-neutral test process/server harness plus exact branch inventory, not threshold weakening."
  - created_at: "2026-07-22T04:41:09.309Z"
    author: codex-jellyfin
    text: "Quality rule: coverage work must assert observable behavior and failure paths; no ignore directives, artificial execution-only cases, or duplicated tests."
  - created_at: "2026-08-07T16:39:28.770Z"
    author: codex-jellyfin-coverage-20260807
    text: "Privacy boundary: live credentials, server URL, user/server/media identifiers, raw OpenAPI documents, and payloads stay in environment variables or owner-only ~/.jellyfin-cli. Live tests run only with JELLYFIN_READ_ONLY=1; production code must reject mutations before target requests."
  - created_at: "2026-08-09T21:26:45.645Z"
    author: codex-jellyfin-api-20260809
    text: "{\"constraints\":[\"no coverage exclusions or ignore directives\",\"no synthetic import-only tests\",\"no live Jellyfin mutation\",\"private config only under ~/.jellyfin-cli\",\"no release publication\"],\"date\":\"2026-08-09\",\"decision\":\"Reuse canonical coverage feature rather than create a duplicate roadmap item\",\"kind\":\"decision\",\"rationale\":\"All API discovery, structured output, setup, official version discovery, generic operation execution, and Jellyfin 12 preview controls already have closed linked plans; repository-wide genuine coverage remains open and blocks static-analysis/docstring enforcement.\"}"
